---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="About | Cloud Architect Lab">
  <section class="page-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">ABOUT</p>

    <h1>Building Architecture Through Practice</h1>

    <p>
      Cloud Architect Lab was created by Rick P., an enterprise technology
      professional with experience across healthcare IT, enterprise imaging,
      infrastructure operations, networking, technical consulting, and
      mission-critical systems.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Why Cloud Architect Lab Exists</h2>

    <p>
      My goal is to develop deeper cloud and AI architecture capability through
      practical engineering work—not certifications alone.
    </p>

    <p>
      Instead of producing disconnected demos, Cloud Architect Lab provides a
      repeatable structure for understanding requirements, evaluating design
      tradeoffs, implementing infrastructure, validating outcomes, and
      communicating architecture clearly.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>The Engineering Approach</h2>

    <p>
      Each case study is treated as a small engineering engagement. The work
      begins with requirements and architecture, continues through
      implementation and validation, and ends with documented lessons that can
      improve future designs.
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>Define the problem before choosing services.</li>
      <li>Model stable architectural concepts before implementation details.</li>
      <li>Record decisions, alternatives, risks, and deferred capabilities.</li>
      <li>Implement approved designs through Infrastructure as Code.</li>
      <li>Validate deployed resources against documented intent.</li>
      <li>Publish useful lessons rather than accomplishments alone.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Areas of Focus</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>AWS cloud architecture</li>
      <li>Enterprise networking</li>
      <li>Terraform and reusable infrastructure patterns</li>
      <li>Cloud security and trust boundaries</li>
      <li>AI-assisted engineering workflows</li>
      <li>Healthcare and other regulated environments</li>
      <li>Architecture documentation and Knowledge as Code</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Current Direction</h2>

    <p>
      Cloud Architect Lab is expanding from foundational AWS networking into
      reusable cloud platforms, AI architecture, automation, and agent-assisted
      engineering workflows.
    </p>

    <div class="button-group">
      <a class="button" href="/case-studies">
        Explore Case Studies →
      </a>

      <a
        class="button button-secondary"
        href="https://github.com/cloudarchitectlab"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noreferrer"
      >
        View GitHub →
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>